    "result": {
     "path": "CONTEXT.md",
     "text": "# acme-web\n\nThe storefront for Acme, rebuilt on the new design system (@acme/tokens and @acme/ui).\n\n## Where things are\n\n- `apps/web`: the Next.js storefront\n- `packages/ui`: shared components\n- `packages/tokens`: colours, type and spacing\n\n## Now\n\nThe checkout's Apple Pay button (T12), search ranking (T14) and the image CDN move (T15, in review).\n"
    }
   },
   {
    "params": {
     "path": "MEMORY.md",
     "project": "acme-web"
    },
    "result": {
     "path": "MEMORY.md",
     "text": "# Memory\n\n- [Design system](memory/design-system.md): tokens first, no raw colours\n- [Checkout](memory/checkout.md): payments go through the billing-api\n- [Testing](memory/testing.md): run the cart tests three times before calling them fixed\n"
    }
   },
   {
    "params": {
     "path": "memory/design-system.md",
     "project": "acme-web"
    },
    "result": {
     "path": "memory/design-system.md",
     "text": "# Design system\n\n## Decided\n\n- Every colour comes from `@acme/tokens`; a raw hex in a component fails lint.\n- Dark mode follows the system setting; there is no in-app switch (user, 2026-10-24).\n\n## Watch out\n\n- The high-contrast set is its own token file: a new token needs a value there too.\n"
    }
   },
   {
    "params": {
     "path": "memory/checkout.md",
     "project": "acme-web"
    },
    "result": {
     "path": "memory/checkout.md",
     "text": "# Checkout\n\n## Decided\n\n- Payments go through billing-api's `/charges`, never Stripe directly from the web app.\n- Apple Pay shows only on Safari with a card in the wallet.\n\n## Ruled out\n\n- A one-page checkout: the address step stays separate for tax.\n"
    }
   },
   {
    "params": {
     "path": "memory/testing.md",
     "project": "acme-web"
    },
    "result": {
     "path": "memory/testing.md",
     "text": "# Testing\n\n- `pnpm test` runs everything; `pnpm test --filter web` just the storefront.\n- The cart tests are timing-sensitive: run them **three times** before calling one fixed (T16).\n"
    }
   }
